Students take the lead in Zhejiang University Academic Annual Conference, and research results are mind-blowing - Xinhuanet
Wash hands with air, detect diseases by blowing, and accurately search for sources of haze. Yesterday evening, a series of groundbreaking academic achievements were recognized at the opening ceremony of the 2016 Academic Annual Conference of Zhejiang University.
The main researchers of these achievements are students, and the research covers environmental, mechanical, energy, medical, life science, humanities education and other major fields. The students started from a curious idea and created many high-end inventions with application value, some of which have won awards at home and abroad.
Biological sensors: your home health check doctor
The team of Zhang Diming, a doctoral student in the School of Biomedical Engineering, demonstrated a smart phone-based biosensor on site, which is only half the size of a smartphone.
"You just need to breathe gently, and this instrument can initially detect your health condition from the composition of your exhaled gas. "
Zhang Diming said that this set of sensors is connected to a smartphone, and after exhaling, the health report will be displayed on the phone.
Smart bracelets on the market that can detect health conditions generally detect physical parameters such as temperature and pulse.
This biosensor uses graphene, a new material, and its target is chemical elements. Its sensitive “sense of smell” allows it to reflect the health condition more deeply and accurately.
Smart surgical lights: doctors' high-powered eyes
In addition to smartphones, smart surgical lights have also been used in operating rooms.
This invention won the silver award at the 44th International Exhibition of Inventions in Geneva, Switzerland this year.
The team of Zhu Linjing and Shen Junfei, master students from the School of Optoelectronic Science and Engineering, started a new idea in the defects of traditional surgical lights and invented the smart LED shadowless surgical lamp.
"Many diseases early detection and removal are not in place, which is related to the light used by doctors in the operating room. "
Shen Junfei said that for example, when cancer is detected early, if doctors cannot see all tumor tissues in time, then cancer cells will still spread.
The smart surgical lamp has four light discs, which can enhance the contrast of different tissues under illumination by adjusting the spectrum.
During the surgery, doctors can adjust the size of the light spot, brightness, spectrum, color uniformity and shadowless rate at any time according to surgical needs and personal habits.
This smart surgical lamp has been tested in hospitals such as the Affiliated Shaoyang Hospital of Zhejiang University School of Medicine and the Affiliated Children's Hospital of Zhejiang University School of Medicine, and has received good feedback.
Last October, this invention won the first prize of National Challenge Cup.
Washing hands with air: water-saving and cool
Ordinary people wash their hands by running water, at most they will use some soap or hand sanitizer, while Li Qizhang and his classmates invented a set of "air handwashing device".
As soon as we step onto the washbasin of the device, our weight compresses the air out.
"It's like a pump.
The compressed air forms a fluid at the tap and combines with water.
In this way, we can wash our hands clean! "
The results of the colour reaction and bacterial residue tests show that the effect of washing hands in this way is the same as that of ordinary hand washing.
This device only needs to rely on our own gravity as a drive, which can ensure the degree of washing and save 90% of water. The whole process is completely energy-free, energy-saving and environmental protection.
Last year, at the Second Global Summit on Grand Challenges, this invention stood out among many world-class universities and won the only gold award.
