Chongqing Vocational Schools Pilot Modern Apprenticeship System, Students Become Employees After Enrollment - Xinhuanet
Yesterday, the reporter learned from the Municipal Education Commission that starting from this year, our city will pilot the "modern apprenticeship" talent training model in 60 secondary vocational schools. Students who are trained in the pilot will have the status of apprentices and will be pre-recorded as unit employees by the pilot enterprises after enrollment.
The Municipal Education Commission requires that the enrollment and admission of secondary vocational schools and the employment procedures of enterprises should be standardized, the dual identities of apprentices as students in secondary vocational schools and quasi-employees of enterprises should be clarified, and the apprentices, schools and enterprises should sign a tripartite agreement according to the principle of two-way selection. For apprentices who are over 16 years old but under 18 years old, the apprentices, guardians, schools and enterprises should sign an agreement to determine the rights and interests of all parties and the specific positions, teaching content, rights and interests protection, etc. of apprentices on the job.
Pilot schools are encouraged to adopt the modern apprenticeship system and jointly carry out pre-job training and post-position training for enterprise employees with cooperative enterprises.
The pilot schools should reform the talent training model.
The school and the enterprise jointly design talent training programs, jointly establish professional teaching standards, curriculum standards, post standards, enterprise master standards, quality control standards and corresponding implementation plans.
The pilot is carried out in one cycle of training, and the internship time of students in enterprises is determined according to the professional talent training plan. The on-the-job internship is generally six months.
In enterprise practice, the enterprise team management model should be implemented. According to the characteristics of different majors, one master can take 2-5 apprentices to form a study group to ensure that students are proficient in the skills required for each rotation training post.
According to the arrangement, from 2016 to August 2019, our city will determine 60 municipal-level vocational schools in three batches to carry out the modern apprenticeship system pilot, with about 50 people in each pilot, and a total of about 3,000 students (apprentices).
In accordance with the principle of piloting first and then implementing, from point to surface, gradually promoting, explore the establishment of long-term mechanism for joint recruitment, joint training, and integrated education between schools and enterprises, and effectively improve students' job skills, and improve the employment rate and quality of students.
