Jiangxi will train 10,000 rural primary school music, physical education and art teachers within three years - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Nanchang, May 22 (Reporter Chen Yushan) The reporter learned from the Jiangxi Provincial Department of Education that in order to enhance the guarantee ability of the shortage of teachers and achieve balanced development of rural compulsory education, since 2016, Jiangxi Province plans to train 1 qualified music teacher, 1 qualified art teacher and 1 qualified physical education teacher for each primary school in rural areas (townships and below) in the province within three years, totaling 10,000.
It is understood that this training was aimed at teachers in primary schools in rural areas of Jiangxi Province under 45 years old who have knowledge or talent in music, art and sports, and can also teach music, art and sports courses.
Through training, they will master the basic knowledge and teaching skills of music, physical education and art subjects, update their teaching ideas and concepts, master modern teaching methods, improve their ability to teach music, physical education and art, activity design ability, campus culture ability and self-development ability, build a team of teachers with one specialty and multiple abilities in music, physical education and art, and alleviate the problem of lack of music, physical education and art teachers in rural areas.
To ensure the quality and effect of the training, Jiangxi also plans to train 100 music, art and physical education teachers in 100 counties (cities and districts) in the province, a total of 300 trainers, to comprehensively improve their teaching demonstration leadership ability, teaching research activity design and organization ability, training ability, network research workshop construction ability, and to play the role of teaching, demonstration, guidance and supervision.
