In fact, there are many things to consider when dressing up for girls who are slightly overweight.
Girls with bigger bodies should not wear skirts that are too short or too long, but rather skirts that are about knee-length and cover the fat part of the thighs.
A skirt that is too short will show off any excess on your legs.
If it is too long, it will make you look short and fat.
If you wear three different colors, you will look taller. The upper body, skirt and stockings are different colors, which will give you a sense of elongation.
In fact, many dark-colored clothes are the standard for slightly overweight girls (the author has deep experience in this), and dark colors are also a good way to cover your body fat. The noble and elegant black skirt is also the first choice for slightly overweight girls.
Wearing dark colors, especially black skirts, can make you look slimmer.
If you have thick calves, don't wear socks and shoes that draw attention to them.
The more popular, the better. The color should not be too bright.
This is to prevent people from getting a sense of obesity when they notice your legs and feet.
For slightly overweight girls, it is necessary to talk about the tricks of clothing matching.
A slightly plump girl should not wear tight skirts. The top should not be too short or tucked into the skirt. It will make people feel uncomfortable. If your legs are thick, you can wear black long stockings or grid socks (the kind with fine checkered patterns). Choose a soft textured printed flared skirt and match it with a loose blouse to cover up the shortcomings of a plump girl.
Of course, the slightly overweight girls also have their own rules when wearing short skirts.
If you're a short girl with a fuller figure, you should choose tops that match the color of your skirt, which will make your shorter stature appear taller.
A short skirt with high heels can make your legs look longer, which is the most fashionable combination in summer!
If you are a big upper body but have thin legs, it is recommended to choose a short dress with a gorgeous style.
It not only covers your big belly, but also shows your strengths.
A-line skirts can make you look thinner, and are more suitable for fat girls. You should choose a tight top to create a layered effect that will make you look thinner.
A simple white T-shirt paired with a skirt, fat MM can also try.
A slightly plump girl can also wear fashion.
As long as you can master the rules of dressing, then slightly overweight girls will be the focus of attention.
After changing my dressing style, I should also exercise more in my daily life and strive to get rid of the label of a slightly overweight girl one day 😄
The 18th World Beverage Innovation Awards (WBIAs) is an award jointly organized by FoodBev Media and the International Beer, Brewing & Beverage Industry Exhibition in Nuremberg, Germany (Brau Beviale).
It attracted 279 works from 25 countries and 22 different categories.
The finalists were announced on October 15 and the winner will be announced online on November 11 (British Summer Time).
We saw that the LP28 sugar-free yogurt of Yuanqi Forest was shortlisted for the Best Dairy Drink Award, the “GOGO Wuhan” marketing of Yili Amulie was shortlisted for the Best Marketing Campaign, and the packaging of the cooperation between PepsiCo and People’s Daily New Media was also shortlisted for the Best Packaging Design/Label Award.
Laura Nettle, senior marketing director at FoodBev Media, said: "We are delighted to celebrate the 18th anniversary of the annual World Beverage Innovation Awards with Brau Beviale.
From new flavours, concepts and functions to brands, packaging and manufacturing, we have seen trends in the beverage industry as the industry continues to innovate in more sustainable ways.
The World Beverage Innovation Awards recognize the most ambitious new products and new developments from established and emerging brands in the global beverage industry this year.
Here is the full list of finalists in each category.
Ardagh Group's technology allows 100% recycled glass to be remelted into new bottles.
The bagged water in the box is packaged with 100% recyclable packaging boxes, which can reduce packaging by 66% and carbon emissions by 97%.
LatCub is 100% biodegradable, uses less paper and does not use environmentally harmful glue or tape.
Ardagh Group's technology allows 100% recycled glass to be remelted and made into new bottles.
The final list of winners will be announced on November 11 (British Summer Time) on FoodBev Media's YouTube channel. FBIF will continue to report on this event. Stay tuned!
