Xinhua All-media + | Beijing Youth Ice Hockey League Helps to Ignite the Olympic Winter Games - Xinhuanet
On December 11, Beijing DreamING team player Pang Yaotian (middle) took a shot during the game.
On the same day, the 2021-2022 Beijing Youth Ice Hockey Club League continued to compete in major ice rinks in Beijing.
This league is divided into regular season and playoffs. The age range of participating athletes is from U6 to U18. The group setting is divided into competitive groups and selection groups, attracting nearly 3,600 players from 256 teams in the city.
After more than 10 years of development, the Beijing Youth Ice Hockey Club League has become a platform for Beijing youth ice hockey enthusiasts to hone their skills and make friends, and has also provided excellent players for the Beijing Youth Ice Hockey Team and the youth team.
The league will play a role in promoting ice hockey among young people in Beijing, fueling enthusiasm for ice hockey in the Winter Olympics, and laying a foundation for the development of ice hockey in Beijing after the Winter Olympics.
Girl raises money for sister by being a target for arrows: "I thought it was just a flesh wound" - Xinhuanet
A girl in Hangzhou Wulin Square stood in front of a large wooden board, which was written with "human target, 10 yuan for one arrow".
Yesterday morning, a photo of "Hangzhou girl willing to be 'target' for her sister to raise money" went viral on WeChat Moments.
The photo shows a girl standing in front of a large wooden board slightly taller than a person in Wulin Square, Hangzhou, with the words "human target, 10 yuan per arrow" written on it, indicating that pedestrians can use bows and arrows to shoot after payment.
This behavior has sparked heated discussion among netizens.
Last night, the publicity chief of Xihu Branch of Hangzhou Public Security Bureau confirmed to the reporter of Beijing News that the police confirmed that the girl made such extreme actions for her sister's donation, but this behavior is not worth advocating, and after being warned, the girl left the local police station yesterday.
Girl "target" for street fundraising admonished
In the picture that was spread on the Internet, a long-haired girl stood in front of a large wooden board in the shape of "person", and the words "human target, 10 yuan per arrow" were written in black ink on the wooden board. There was her bank account number and WeChat and Alipay accounts on another wooden board in front of her.
The image has caused controversy since it was posted online.
Some netizens believed that this was "a begging behavior to attract attention", while many netizens expressed sympathy for it.
"We found this situation when we patrolled near the square at about 10 a.m. on the 23rd, and there were already quite a few onlookers. "
The police officers of Tianshui Police Station near the incident site said in an interview with local media that there were two girls who set up stalls, both about 20 years old and dressed in a youthful and beautiful way.
Among them, the girl who acted as a "human target" was crying and asked the passers-by to play this game; another girl was shouting on the side, saying that her friend's elder sister had leukemia and needed surgery fee urgently, so she asked for help.
"We contacted the local police in Guizhou and learned that the girl was raising money for her sister's leukemia treatment. "
Last night, the publicity officer of Hangzhou Public Security Bureau Xiacheng Branch told Beijing News that the girl was named Ji Jiali, and she was collecting donations for her sister Ji Jiayan.
However, since the treatment still needs more than 300,000 yuan, he made such an action because he couldn’t think of a good way to raise funds.
He said that in the whole process, one of the two girls served as a target and the other served as an assistant, but did not participate in it. No one was found to shoot arrows in the whole process, but some people watched and took pictures and posted them on Weibo.
After the police department identified the bow and arrow used, it was found that the bow and arrow were not under control.
The person in charge said, "We do not advocate such a way of fundraising to attract attention."
After being warned by the police station officers, she has left the police station.
