What is the hottest in 2021?
Undoubtedly, it is the Tokyo Olympics.
Do you think that only Olympic athletes can win awards?
A few days ago, an article titled "Look! Project managers can win gold medals in Olympic events" was very popular. It mentioned that project managers could be the first in many projects and no one could match them: moving bricks, business trips, staying up late were the daily routine of project managers; fire fighting, taking the blame, apologizing were not a problem.
An article that seems like a joke, but it also reveals the daily hardships of project managers, and behind it is the powerlessness of current project management work.
And those who work in project management are gradually choosing to take some action to get themselves out of the dilemma in their work.
From the annual increase in PMP (International Certified Project Management Professional Qualification) registration numbers, it can be seen that more and more project management practitioners have improved their project management capabilities through learning.
According to the “Report on the Development of China’s Project Management in the Past 20 Years (1999-2019)”, as of September 2019, the cumulative number of PMP® applicants nationwide was nearly 600,000, the number of PMP® certified persons was about 420,000, and the number of valid certificate holders was about 300,000, accounting for 31.2% of the total number of PMP® certificates globally.
In the past 10 years, the number of PMP certificate holders has increased year by year, which indicates that more and more project managers have realized that it is no longer possible to rely on simple copying of previous "old experience" to do things, and the ever-changing working environment tells us that we should learn how to stand on the shoulders of giants to explore the path ahead.
However, does obtaining a PMP certification guarantee smooth project management?
Many beginners in project management say that by studying PMP/IPMP and other related courses, they can systematically master the ten areas of project management and five process groups and other related knowledge points, but when they actually carry out project management work, they are still confused.
Many project managers often feedback the following problems: the project management awareness is not in place, they simply rely on personal experience, and they have project management theory but do not know how to practice; there is no systematic project management process and system support, so it is impossible to implement the work, project estimation is inaccurate, and the control degree is poor, so the project is delayed again and again; the division of labor among members is unclear, and the “old oil” in the team does not know how to deal with it; the cross-departmental assistance communication is not smooth, and the project is difficult to promote...
Therefore, Zhongtian Huaxia Consulting, which has focused on product innovation and R&D management for more than a decade, has helped many excellent enterprises to train a large number of key R&D talents such as product managers and project managers, and has won honorary titles such as "China Enterprise R&D Management Talent Training Demonstration Base". It has brought the online course "R&D Project Manager Special Training Camp".
The online course of "Special Training Camp for R&D Project Managers" is a way of online fragmented learning. It combines the practical cases, tools and methods of many R&D enterprises to help you master the knowledge and standard actions required for project managers and take the advanced path of project management.
This is also an opportunity to promote the training process of project managers with lower costs and less investment, and bring high-efficiency operation results for enterprises.
Without evidence, you can first see how other students evaluate this course: This course is not only taught by Zhongtian Huaxia expert team (former Huawei R&D management team), combined with international advanced project management methodology and many well-known enterprises real business scenarios, to give a professional explanation of the course content in simple terms.
It will also provide scientific and practical management tools and methods, as well as rich templates and forms to help students apply what they have learned in class to their specific work after class.
