JETC Credit Advocates Reasonable Consumption for Consumers on the Eve of “Singles’ Day” - Economic Observer - A Professional Financial News Website
This year’s “Singles’ Day” carnival saw a total transaction amount of RMB1.77 trillion in online payment business across the country, setting a new record compared to previous years.
The dazzling variety of discount red envelopes and the eye-catching live shopping have once again made consumers shout that they have benefited from it. On one hand, this wave of consumption has made people sigh at the growing national purchasing power, but on the other hand, it is also necessary to cool down and think about the impact of consumerism on society and contemporary mainstream consumers.
On the eve of “Singles’ Day”, Home Credit Consumer Finance Co., Ltd. (hereinafter referred to as “Home Credit”) issued a rational consumption advocacy, reminding users, especially young people, to establish good consumption awareness and consumption habits, and to refuse blind consumption and excessive consumption.
According to the results of the "Consumer Financial Literacy Survey and Analysis Report" released by the People's Bank of China this year, the national consumer financial literacy index is 66.81, which has increased by 2.04 compared with 2019.
Overall, the performance of Chinese residents in financial consumption is relatively good, but there are significant differences in different aspects of financial behavior and skills, and the level of basic financial knowledge needs to be further improved.
The financial literacy of the elderly and young people is relatively low, and "the elderly and young" will still be the key objects of continuous attention in financial education; the "Report on the Debt Situation of Chinese Youth" released by Nielsen and the "2019-2020 China Youth Consumption Report" released by CCTV Finance show that the younger generation has great consumption potential, credit consumption has become an important way to upgrade consumption, 86.6% of young people are using credit products, nearly half of them have no debt accumulation, although the younger generation shows a rational consumption trend overall, which is very different from the "excessive spending" label attached by the outside world, but some young people do have excessive consumption and follow-up consumption behavior, and thus have too much financial pressure and debt risk, and even lead to gradual increase in social problems, financial enterprises should be brave in taking social responsibility and positive guidance.
As a licensed consumer finance institution, Home Credit has been committed to helping people build their own happy life with high-quality and considerate services, advocating that consumers establish good and correct consumption concepts, and actively responding to regulatory calls to enhance the rational consumption awareness of consumers, especially young people, with practical actions.
Over the past few years, China Credit Suisse has continuously carried out all-round and diverse financial knowledge popularization activities for young people including college students, and through cooperation with top domestic universities, it has launched various forms of innovation practice competitions to subtly guide the consumption needs of young people, help them establish rational consumption concepts, plan their consumption needs, and then help them accumulate wealth in life.
On the occasion of the 12.12 shopping festival, Home Credit reminds all consumers to establish a reasonable consumption awareness and a correct view of money, resist blind consumption and excessive consumption, and avoid the misunderstanding of consumer loans, so as not to affect personal credit and future economic life.
You must plan in advance when consuming, and repay on time according to your ability.
If overdue, the overdue record will be recorded in the personal credit report, which may have a bad impact on future car buying, house buying and other economic life.
At the same time, when enjoying financial products and services, it is also necessary to choose formal institutions and channels, and pay attention to check whether the relevant institutions have the qualifications to operate.
In the future, CITIC Consumer Finance will continue to leverage its mature and reliable consumer finance system and constantly update and iterate its financial products to provide consumers with more personalized and diversified services, continuously help the public improve their financial knowledge, help consumers cultivate the concept of rational consumption and moderate borrowing, and become a consumer’s lifelong trusted consumer finance partner.
