Iranian President: If sanctions against Iran are lifted, Iran's nuclear negotiations are expected to reach an agreement - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency Teheran, December 11 (Reporters Gao Wencheng and Wang Shoubao) Iranian President Raisi said on the 11th in Tehran, the capital of Iran, that if the United States lifted sanctions against Iran, the negotiations on the comprehensive agreement on the Iranian nuclear issue could reach a "good agreement".
According to the news released by the website of the Iranian president, Raisi said at a meeting with Iranian envoys to surrounding countries that Iran had proved its sincerity in negotiations by submitting proposals to other parties involved in the Iran nuclear deal.
If the United States is determined, "the road to reach an agreement will be smooth".
The parties to the Iran nuclear deal began talks in Vienna, the capital of Austria, in April this year to discuss the issue of resuming compliance with the agreement between the United States and Iran.
The new round of talks began in Vienna on November 29 and was temporarily suspended on December 3, and continued on December 9.
