Xi Jinping sends congratulatory letter to the 2021 Bay Area Science Forum - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 11 -- On December 11, President Xi Jinping sent a congratulatory message to the 2021 Greater Bay Area Science Forum.
Xi Jinping pointed out that the world is undergoing a major change unseen in a century, and global scientific and technological innovation has entered a period of intensive activity. A new round of scientific and technological revolution and industrial transformation have had a profound impact on the global economic structure.
The Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area should focus on the strategic positioning of building an international science and technology innovation center, strive to build a global science and technology innovation highland, and promote the development of emerging industries.
China is willing to work with scientists from all over the world and international scientific and technological organizations to closely carry out international scientific and technological exchanges and cooperation, strengthen research on major scientific issues, promote the breakthrough of common scientific and technological problems, deepen collaboration on key scientific projects, jointly promote the development of the world's scientific undertakings, and better benefit mankind.
The 2021 Greater Bay Area Science Forum opened in Guangzhou, Guangdong Province on the same day, with the theme of "Exploring the Future and Sharing Science", and was hosted by the People's Government of Guangdong Province.
