The longest period of time that university students in Guangxi can take a leave of absence to start a business is five years - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Nanning, May 19 (Reporter Zhang Ying) The reporter learned from the Education Department of Guangxi Zhuang Autonomous Region that in the future, Guangxi universities will implement flexible academic systems, relax the length of time for college students to take a break from school, and extend the length of time for students to take a break from school to start a business by 2 to 5 years on the basis of the original academic system. The time taken to take a break from school to start a business can be regarded as practical education time.
In order to promote the improvement of college students' entrepreneurship and innovation ability, Guangxi Education, Human Resources and Social Security and other departments have jointly built an entrepreneurial platform, built more off-campus practice teaching bases for college students, university science parks, college students' business parks, business incubation bases, etc., and provided external guarantees for college students' entrepreneurship.
According to the requirements, by 2020, the area of innovation and entrepreneurship practice base of each university should reach more than 30,000 square meters for undergraduate schools and more than 20,000 square meters for vocational schools.
The government encourages colleges and universities to establish innovation and entrepreneurship credits, and gives priority to supporting students who perform excellently in innovation and entrepreneurship practice to change their majors.
Teachers in colleges and universities should spend at least two months every two years to work in industry enterprises for job training, so as to improve their awareness and ability of entrepreneurship and innovation education.
The Education Department of the autonomous region requires all colleges and universities in Guangxi to implement the innovation and entrepreneurship training plan for college students, and strive to make every college student participate in an innovation and entrepreneurship training plan during their school years.
Colleges and universities should actively organize students to participate in various innovation and entrepreneurship competitions at all levels, and provide financial support.
NEWS GOV-MO: UM Honours Seven Distinguished Persons with Honorary Doctorates
The University of Macau (UM) held the "2021 Honorary Degree and Advanced Degree Award Ceremony" today (11), awarding honorary doctorates to Liu Zunyi, Chen Kaixian, Shuji Nakamura, Li Lanjuan, Li Xiaoliang, Zhu Lilan and Jiang Zhaohui in recognition of their outstanding achievements and significant contributions to the development of society and education.
At the award ceremony, Chief Executive and representative of the University of Macau Council, Secretary for Social Affairs and Culture Ouyang Yu presented honorary doctorate degrees in the presence of President of the University of Macau Council, Lin Jin Cheng, and President of the University of Macau, Song Yonghua.
Professor Liu Zunyi was awarded an honorary Doctor of Education, Professor Chen Kaixian was awarded an honorary Doctor of Science, Professor Nakamura Shuji was awarded an honorary Doctor of Science, Professor Li Lanjuan was awarded an honorary Doctor of Science, Professor Li Xiaoliang was awarded an honorary Doctor of Business Administration, Professor Zhu Lilan was awarded an honorary Doctor of Science, and Ms. Jiang Zhaohui was awarded an honorary Doctor of Science.
When delivering his speech, Ouyang Yu first extended warm congratulations and high respect to the seven outstanding individuals who were awarded honorary doctorates, as they have achieved remarkable accomplishments in different fields and made outstanding contributions to the development of the country and the progress of the world; he also expressed his most sincere blessings to graduates and parents, and paid heartfelt respects to the university’s teaching staff team who are devoted to their jobs and have excellent academic skills.
Sun Yifeng, a chair professor of the Faculty of Humanities at the University of Macau, said in his eulogy for Professor Liu Zunyi that Professor Liu Zunyi is a globally renowned economist, known for his outstanding academic achievements and forward-looking educational concepts.
In addition to his achievements in economic development, economic growth and East Asian economy, he was also a visionary educational leader.
In short, he was an outstanding man in so many areas.
When reading the tribute to Shuji Nakamura, Sun Yifeng said that Professor Shuji Nakamura is a pioneer in sustainable energy technology.
He was one of three winners of the 2014 Nobel Prize in Physics for his invention of the blue light-emitting diode (LED).
Professor Nakamura’s invention not only completely changed the lighting industry, but also promoted the production of white light-emitting diodes that are widely used in daily life and industrial production today, making a great contribution to human well-being.
Sun Yifeng read out the praise for Li Lanjuan, saying that Professor Li Lanjuan, as a pioneer of artificial liver in China, created a unique and effective artificial liver system, made major breakthroughs in treating severe hepatitis and liver failure, and significantly reduced the mortality rate of liver failure.
In this battle against COVID-19, the "Four Resistances and Two Balances" plan proposed by her and her team, as well as the three technologies of artificial liver, microecology and stem cells, have significantly increased the treatment rate of severe cases.
When reading the praises of Li Xiaoliang, Sun Yifeng said that Professor Li Xiaoliang laid the foundation for innovative research in operations management, shaped the thinking mode of supply chain theory and practice, and completely changed the business model around the world.
Lee Hsueh-liang is known for popularizing the concept of the whip effect in operations management and exploring measures to counteract it.
In the face of the epidemic and the tense economic situation, the long whip effect has become more prominent, leading to serious disruption of the supply chain.
Li Xiaoliang’s far-sighted research is like a ray of hope in the snow, helping the industry to cope with difficulties, and thus bringing about great social value.
When reading the praises of Zhu Li-lan, Sun Yifeng said that in her scientific research work, she discovered a breakthrough and innovative staining technique for sample preparation, which has a high reputation among domestic and foreign scientific peers.
She was honored with important honorary titles such as academician of the International Eurasian Academy of Sciences for her extraordinary scientific and technological achievements, and won the lofty status that she deserved in the world's science and technology temple with her brilliant achievements.
Chen Xin, the Acting Dean of the UM Institute of Chinese Medical Sciences, read the eulogy of Chen Kai-shin, saying that Professor Chen Kai-shin has been engaged in drug research and development for more than 40 years. His outstanding scientific achievements and important contributions to the country, Macao, the University of Macau, and the national key laboratory have given him a high international status and reputation.
His active role in promoting the development of traditional Chinese medicine in Macao and the Greater Bay Area fully reflects his sense of mission to contribute to the national medicine development strategy.
When Xu Chengzhong, Dean of the University of Macau Institute for Technology, read out Jiang Zhaohui’s eulogy, he said that Ms. Jiang Zhaohui’s major inventions and patents involved in research and development have accumulated more than 15 items related to storage virtualization, navigation, file systems and power management, which are highly practical, widely used, and improve the convenience of human life.
As an accomplished inventor, Ms. Jiang is often able to simplify complex science and theory and make them accessible to the public.
Finally, Chen Kaixian read out the letter of thanks as the representative of honorary doctor.
He was very happy to see that Macao and the Greater Bay Area had set a good example in the medical industry: from the first national key laboratory of quality research of traditional Chinese medicine established by UM to the flourishing development of traditional Chinese medicine in the Greater Bay Area, UM has made great contributions to the integration of outstanding talents in the field of traditional Chinese medicine in the Greater Bay Area.
In addition, he believed that the management team of the University of Macau had far-sightedness, which not only provided fertile ground for students to conduct scientific research in academic terms, but also sent many responsible talents to society.
He was honored to be able to exchange and cooperate with the University of Macau, and he sincerely congratulated the University of Macau on its achievements in recent years.
