As NFTs are rapidly gaining popularity, a new concept has emerged in the crypto community.
In 2021, a blockchain game called Axie Infinity had a huge impact in Southeast Asia, and some residents who lost their jobs due to the pandemic began to earn stable income from this game.
Axie Infinity is a pet-raising game based on blockchain technology, which combines various gameplay, including NFT. It is currently the NFT project with the highest transaction volume, which has exceeded $3 billion.
According to TokenTerminal data, Axie Infinity’s daily revenue exceeds $8.2 million, which is close to that of Honor of Kings.
On August 6 this year, Axie Infinity officially said that its daily active users had exceeded 1 million.
The popularity of Axie Infinity has spread a new “play-to-earn” model to more people. With the help of blockchain and smart contract, players are no longer single characters. In addition to having fun and economic benefits from the game, they can also participate in the governance of the game ecosystem.
This subjectivity is not granted by the game maker, but is guaranteed by blockchain technology.
I was most impressed by a news about my friend’s stock price. The choice of the track, that is, the choice of the target industry, should be based on the following criteria: first, the industry with large growth potential, at least with a market scale of more than 100 billion; second, the industry with good future growth, considering the industry with the best growth in the next 3-5 years; and finally, the industry with policy support.
How wide the track is refers to the market size, how long the track is refers to the development stage of the industry, and whether the track is flat or rough refers to the competitive landscape of the industry.
Cheer for the right track!
In the new year, the first thing is to summarize 2021 and adjust the tactical layout of 2022.
The tactic is to "do the things right", which means doing things right.
The strategy is to "do the right thing", that is, do the right thing.
The strategy is to find the direction, and the tactics are to implement it. Above most tactical thinking, there is room for strategic thinking.
For example, on top of how to increase the number of customers (tactical thinking), we can think about whether to continue to deepen in the current field or expand horizontally (strategic thinking); for example, on top of how to improve customer retention (tactical thinking), we can think about how to improve the retention rate of core customers and high-value customers (strategic thinking); on top of how to improve participation in activities (tactical thinking), we can consider how to set the correct activity KPI, achieve the correct activity goal, such as improving the participation of target customers, activating high-value silent customers, and precise new customers; on top of how to improve DAU (tactical thinking), we can consider whether the current growth is healthy and sustainable.
After 12 years of birth, Bitcoin has welcomed several milestone events in 2021.
On September 7, El Salvador, a small Central American country, designated Bitcoin as its legal tender, marking the first time that Bitcoin has become the legal tender of a country or region.
On October 12, the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission approved ProShares to launch Bitcoin ETFs for the first time in eight years, and list them on the New York Stock Exchange, marking the first compliance Bitcoin futures ETF landing on the American capital market, and the second expansion of the investment exposure of cryptocurrencies.
From the perspective of blockchain technology development, Bitcoin is not the main character.
On November 14, 2021, Bitcoin underwent a soft fork upgrade called "Taproot", which increased the anonymity of Bitcoin network transactions and reduced the data burden in transactions by changing the data structure of the block itself.
