Education news: Beijing compresses the proportion of specialized students in junior high school in 2016 - Xinhuanet
On the 21st and 22nd, the examination for special talents of junior high school students in Beijing was organized and implemented by the Education Committee of each district.
This year, all districts in Beijing have reduced the proportion of students with special talents, and the competition for students with special talents has become more intense.
For example, in Dongcheng District, this year, the proportion of elementary school students entering junior high schools with special skills is generally not more than 5% of the total number of admissions in the district, and the planned number of admissions is 380, but the proportion of students who actually attend school does not exceed 10% of the total number of admissions in the school.
Students with sports, art, and science and technology specialties who registered online are eligible to participate in the special talent enrollment examination.
In order to facilitate students to take the examination nearby, Dongcheng District continued last year's arrangement of the examination, and set up 1-2 examination sites in each school district, a total of 13 examination sites.
The examination points are divided into examination rooms according to the examination areas, and the time periods are divided by hours. The students will enter the examination points on the day of the examination according to the time periods to take the examinations in different examination rooms of the examination areas.
On May 23, the list of students who passed the examination was publicly displayed online by the District Education Enrollment and Examination Center, and students can query the examination results online.
