48 hours of negative nucleic acid, set up a "buffer zone", the State Council joint prevention and control mechanism issued a document to strengthen the epidemic prevention and control in port cities - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 11 (Reporters Dong Ruifeng and Gu Tiancheng) The Joint Prevention and Control Mechanism of the State Council recently issued a notice on strengthening the prevention and control of COVID-19 in port cities, requiring that those who leave land border port cities (except for those connected to Hong Kong and Macao) should hold a negative nucleic acid test certificate within 48 hours, and those who go to land border port cities should have at least one nucleic acid test after arrival.
According to the notice, the above requirements are valid from the date when each province, autonomous region and municipality determines the scope of port cities and announces it to March 15, 2022.
In addition, the notice also proposed that port cities with conditions may study setting up a buffer zone for epidemic prevention and control within their jurisdiction.
According to relevant person in charge of the Disease Prevention and Control Bureau of the National Health Commission, for some port cities, cross-border trade is the main economic pillar of the local economy, and there is frequent exchange between the two sides.
By implementing a differentiated management policy for zones, the prevention and control of the epidemic will be transformed from one line to two lines, which is expected to achieve the forward shift of the checkpoint, compress the risk of epidemic overflow, and achieve the maximum effect of epidemic prevention and control with the minimum social impact and the lowest social cost.
Recently, there have been several outbreaks of local outbreaks in China, which are all imported from overseas epidemics through port cities.
The above-mentioned notice pointed out that this exposed some problems, such as untimely epidemic monitoring and early warning, non-implementation of closed-loop management for high-risk positions, formalities of regular nucleic acid testing, inadequate disinfection in all links of cold-chain items, irregular management of centralized isolation sites, and insufficient scientific and precise emergency handling of the epidemic.
The notice required that efforts should be made in nine aspects, including improving the epidemic prevention and control mechanism in port cities, perfecting the epidemic monitoring and early warning system, and implementing border control measures, to accelerate the shortcomings and weaknesses in the prevention and control of port cities, and to do a good job in prevention and control without slackening and scientifically and accurately, and to weave and tighten the defense line of preventing the import of epidemics.
The notice stressed that the port cities should synchronously study and deploy the epidemic prevention and control and people's livelihood, publish and open the hotline for people's livelihood, regularly investigate the potential risks in the supply of basic living materials, prices, and other aspects, and timely solve and actively respond to the outstanding problems reflected by the masses.
According to the notice, the port cities referred to include the counties (cities, districts, banners) where open land, water and air ports are located, the cities (provinces, autonomous regions, municipalities) where they are located, and the municipalities directly under the Central Government where they are located. The specific scope will be determined by each province (autonomous region, municipalities directly under the Central Government) according to the needs of epidemic prevention and control and announced in a timely manner.
