I accidentally saw the following article, which talks about why this customer wants the logistics company in the bonded area to help with canning from a business perspective and from the perspective of shelf life. Although canning is a deep processing, it does not fall within the scope of the bonded logistics company. The following text may explain why the customer wants to do so.
I went to many milk powder manufacturers and contacted many milk powder production lines.
In fact, the raw materials of bagged and canned milk powder are exactly the same, with no difference at all.
So you may be asking: why is the shelf life of a bag of rice one year, while that of a can is two years or more?
Or ask again: why is there such a big price difference between canned and bagged products?
In fact, from this point of view, many consumers or mothers believe that this is because the raw materials are different, so the quality will be much better.
In fact, the raw materials are the same, but people think that the expensive ones are the good ones.
There are also consumers who have this mentality and after eating, they say that the taste or flavor of the canned food is different!
Now, let me tell you why canned food is expensive. What makes it expensive?
Why is there such a big price difference between them if they have the same raw materials?
Because when manufacturers set prices, they usually take into account that if the bag price is too high, consumers will find it difficult to accept, which means that the manufacturer's profit is low or even no profit. So what can the manufacturer rely on for survival?
So they have a big increase in pricing for their cans to ensure their profit margin.
Therefore, most manufacturers promote canned goods rather than bagged goods.
And the manufacturers that you think of, they spend tens of millions or even hundreds of millions on advertising every year. Where does this money come from?
You can imagine.
As society develops, the market promotion costs, such as: the promotion staff of shopping malls, the display costs of shopping malls, the product gift costs, and the advertising costs are also increasing.
So, various manufacturers are constantly adding new products, and they are canned, and their prices are constantly rising. In fact, these are new products that come out with the increase of market costs.
The main purpose is to obtain higher profits, but in fact, their raw material cost will not exceed 3 or 4 yuan.
There are also some brands that, in order to promote their products, will do anything to link up with hospital doctors and ask them to assist in promoting their products, taking a profit ranging from 30 yuan to 80 yuan from each bottle.
However, China’s relevant laws absolutely do not allow such operation methods. In fact, this kind of practice is to cheat consumers.
It is recommended that you buy canned milk powder and put it into a can, which can save money, increase the preservation and sealing of milk powder, and have no effect on children.
Also, don’t think that the shelf life of canned food is longer than that of bagged food. If the shelf life of canned food and bagged food is the same after opening the can, it is just that the bagged food is not easy to preserve after opening the bag, and it is easy to be affected by moisture and spoil.
