Is it electric leakage if feet are numb after soaking in a foot bath basin?
Choosing an appropriate foot bath can play a good foot therapy and health care role. Today, Guomei editor will answer this question to help friends.
As people’s awareness of health care has increased, foot bath basins have become increasingly popular among consumers. A large number of products with different grades have emerged in the market, ranging from more than 100 yuan to thousands of yuan, giving consumers a lot of choice.
According to relevant data, compared with traditional home appliances, health care appliances such as foot baths have been very popular in sales, but there is no specific industry standard for foot baths, so there is a certain level of safety hazard.
"It's really dangerous to soak your feet in charged water!"
Mr. Li told reporters that he bought a foot bath basin for his father as a birthday present, but his father felt numbness in his feet when soaking his feet.
Mr. Li first thought that it was caused by the vibration function of the foot bath tub, but he did not expect that his father still felt numbness in his feet after turning off the vibration function.
Mr. Li tried the electric pen, and the pen was lit. Mr. Li was surprised to find that the water in the foot bath basin was electrically charged.
Later, he contacted the merchant, and the merchant's attitude was not bad. Although he returned the foot bath basin, Mr. Li still felt unhappy.
He found that there was no clear and detailed industry regulations for the hot tubs which have been popular for a long time, including the maximum temperature setting, the target group, and the material guaranteeing non-toxicity.
However, in general, foot bath basins do not have electricity problems, but it is not excluded that a small number of products are not strictly controlled at the time of leaving the factory.
Therefore, when purchasing, choose a split foot bath basin.
The water and electricity are separated, so there is no safety hazard.
At the same time, you can test it with a tester.
The 13th Provincial Tea Expo opens - Video Headlines - Hunan Daily Online - Huasheng Online
Hunan Daily, December 10 (full-media reporter Zhang Shangwu, Hu Panpan, correspondent Liu Xiaoling, photographer Li Jian) This morning, the 13th Hunan Tea Industry Exposition and Xiangxi Red Tea Promotion Conference was held at the Hunan International Convention and Exhibition Center, showcasing the tea industry, innovating tea technology, promoting tea culture, and accelerating the sprint to achieve the goal of a tea industry worth RMB100 billion.
Hou Shunli, Vice President of the Council of the All-China Federation of Supply and Marketing Cooperatives, and Ye Hongzhuan, Vice Chairman of the Standing Committee of the Provincial People's Congress, attended the opening ceremony.
Professor Liu Zhonghua, an academician of the Chinese Academy of Engineering, made a grand recommendation at the opening ceremony: the source of red tea is in Xinhua, and the rise of red tea has injected new impetus into the "five-colored Hunan tea".
In recent years, the Provincial Party Committee and the Provincial Government have strongly supported the development of tea industry, promoted the construction of a 100 billion yuan Hunan tea industry, and formed a development pattern of "three Hunan and four waters and five-color tea".
The tea industry in the province has increased innovation, and green tea, black tea, red tea and other main tea categories have been launched in turn, and the main tea production areas have promoted the integration of tea and tourism to promote the income of tea farmers.
The fortune wheel turns, and black tea is back in force.
Experts in the tea industry in the province said that after picking green tea, picking red tea and black tea, tea farmers have income in all four seasons, and the output value of tea gardens has increased sharply.
At the opening ceremony, provincial leaders awarded the fourth batch of enterprises authorized to use the "Hunan Red Tea" trademark, and Xinhua was awarded the title of "Source of Hunan Red Tea".
At the Xin Hua Red Tea Exhibition Hall, Fujian tea merchants were interested in a high mountain tea called “Ice Spring”, and immediately placed an order.
Wang Zhun, secretary-general of the Provincial Tea Industry Association, said happily that the current epidemic and other factors have affected the tea market to varying degrees, but from the tea expo site, there are many highlights.
The new Hua black tea is a touch of red, which injects the connotation of tea culture, and the popularity and transaction are booming. The Hunan tea industry is welcoming a new spring.
