Ding Zilin: To a friend.
I would like to express my heartfelt gratitude to all friends for their humanitarian assistance over the long period of more than 30 years after our relatives died, especially since I had issued a call for humanitarian assistance to domestic and foreign friends in my personal name in early 1994, the assistance has not been interrupted so far.
Nowadays, most of the parents of the victims have passed away, and the orphans have grown up and got married and found jobs.
It is your generosity that has helped us through the most difficult of times.
At present, the COVID-19 pandemic is raging around the world, and most of the donors are already retired.
Therefore, I earnestly request you to suspend the humanitarian donation to our group of Tiananmen Mothers, and this humanitarian assistance activity should have been perfectly ended long ago.
I will always remember your love and firmly believe that your righteous deeds will be remembered in history.
For various reasons, I can only express my wishes in this way, so please understand!
Please accept my sincere best wishes.
Tao said: I would like to take this opportunity to introduce the history of 32 years of humanitarian assistance carried out by the International Federation of Chinese Students and Scholars (IFCSS) and the Minnesota China Democracy Foundation (MCDF).
During the process of humanitarian assistance, the American Chinese Relief Association and the Minnesota China Democratic Foundation are two parallel organizations, and their project executors often have cross-overs.
(Apple Daily picture: The Tiananmen Mothers website is managed by Tao Ye.) pic.twitter.com/UxID9ZGjzm
The relief funds often fail to reach the hands of the relatives of June 4th victims.
In 1994, at the suggestion of Teacher Ding, a special group was established by the "Tiananmen Mothers" to coordinate and be responsible for the reception and distribution of humanitarian relief funds.
In 1998, the MCDF established the "June 4 Orphan Education Fund". After 11 years of implementation, in 2009, after all the June 4 orphans graduated from university, the MCDF then established the "June 4 Orphan and Elderly Poor Relief Fund", which has been implemented to this day.
The funding for these projects comes mainly from campus and community donations from the year of the Tiananmen Square massacre, generous donations from individuals, and support from the Foundation for Democracy at Sister Universities.
Since 2018, it has also received support from the Reform Through Research Foundation.
Until last year, after 31 years, the victims of the June 4th Movement finally received a portion of the donations collected in Hong Kong in the name of the June 4th Movement.
During this period, China Human Rights also independently implemented their humanitarian relief projects.
We understand that Mr. Ding stopped the donation for June 4th is for the donors. We are indeed some retired people, and our income is not as abundant as before retirement. We would like to express our gratitude to Mr. Ding's letter "To a Friend".
We will respect the decision of the families and end the project within two years, and resume it immediately if needed.
I would like to express my gratitude and respect to those brave comrades who have been generous and risked their lives to deliver humanitarian aid for years.
