The cover plate of the microfluidic chip is made of PC material, so do not allow solvents that react chemically with PC to pass through.
Do not use a hand pump syringe to directly inject the chip, otherwise it is easy to cause leakage.
Microfluidic chips with common substrates are tested by pure water at an injection pressure of 500 mbar (100 um channel depth) or 300 mbar (50 um channel depth) before shipment.
The chip on glass is tested with pure water at an injection pressure of 800 mbar (100 um channel) before shipment. Please be careful not to collide with sharp objects during use, or the substrate may be damaged.
Please consider the viscosity of the solution during use and do not exceed this range, otherwise leakage will occur.
For microfluidic microchips with common substrates, we suggest that the flow rate should be set below 150ul/min under the condition of pure water injection by a syringe pump, and the flow rate of oil phase should be set below 50ul/min.
Please consider the viscosity of the actual injection liquid and increase your flow rate parameter value from slow to fast.
After the experiment is completed, please clean the internal channel of the general chip in time, otherwise it is easy to cause blockage.
Microfluidic chips are consumables and cannot be used repeatedly for a long time.
If the chip is damaged due to long-term use or improper operation, it will not be exchanged or returned.
If you need microfluidic chips that can withstand greater pressure or flow rate, please contact our customer service for customization.
