A programming novice who wants to share his personal experience.
If you plan to enter this industry, you can choose to find a place for training, but if you don’t have such an idea, it is better to study by yourself. After all, the cost of training is very high, and you will need 6 months to learn.
But if you are planning to get into this industry, training is really a very good choice, especially for those with very weak self-control, training is even better.
If you have a strong self-control, you can also choose to study on your own, but it will be more tiring.
Of course, choosing a good training institution is very important.
First, we should look at the faculty strength of the institution. If the faculty strength is not strong enough, this training institution is meaningless. Of course, some newly opened training institutions do not have particularly strong faculty strength.
Secondly, you should find out about the training institution before you choose it. It is best to find out about the students who have graduated from the institution. After all, only the students of the institution know how the institution is and whether the courses are good or bad.
Hello, actually I don't know how to answer your question because you didn't introduce your own situation, and learning this thing has a lot to do with personal situation.
For example, your specialty, age, the language you want to learn, and even the city you are in, all of these things are related to the industry you are studying or want to work in.
If you are a student and have not graduated yet, or if you are a computer major and have graduated, then I personally recommend self-study if you have enough time. This is the most efficient and cost-effective method. Many offline and online training institutions are actually very good, but the cost of learning is high, and the time investment is relatively large. Basically, you need to concentrate on training for 3-6 months.
However, if I am the one who said these things, self-study is very convenient. Many learning resources on the Internet are free now, or there are also many training resources on Bilibili. If you don’t know how to find resources, you can contact me through the introduction to get free resources, or you can also consult in detail.
There are also some classic books that can be combined with video to provide a comprehensive learning experience.
If you are not a computer professional, but can afford to pay for the cost of learning and time, it is recommended to go to a training institution to study. This way, you will not have to work hard, the teacher will explain in detail, and there will be someone to answer your questions. In addition, it will also help with learning planning or supervision.
And now many training institutions will sign employment agreements and have internal promotion quotas. After learning, they will be recommended to companies, so this can save a lot of time in the interview process for finding work.
These are my views. As I don’t know your situation, I only gave a general introduction and didn’t go into details. If you have any other questions, you can contact me at any time for communication.
