Yunnan: Coordinated and standardized management of rural public welfare positions - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Kunming, December 12 (Reporter Lin Bifeng) In order to continue to do a good job in employment assistance for people who have been lifted out of poverty and consolidate and expand the achievements of poverty alleviation, Yunnan Province has recently issued relevant policies on promoting rural revitalization and management of public welfare positions in villages, which will help promote the comprehensive revitalization of rural areas.
According to the relevant person in charge of the Yunnan Provincial Human Resources and Social Security Department, at present, Yunnan has developed a total of 448,300 rural public welfare posts, which are used to place poverty-stricken labor force and other rural disadvantaged groups, and play an important role in helping the poverty-stricken people to increase their income, consolidate the achievements of poverty eradication, and effectively improve the public service capabilities of the villages.
This new regulation was jointly issued by seven departments in Yunnan Province, including the Human Resources and Social Security Bureau, Rural Revitalization Bureau, and Finance Bureau. It mainly standardizes the scope of recruitment for village-level public welfare positions, fund management, position development, and position management.
In terms of post development and setting, the new rules clearly state that the posts should be set up in accordance with the principles of "post setting according to needs, determining personnel according to posts, dynamic management, total quantity control", "whoever develops, whoever uses, whoever is responsible" and "one person, one post, voluntary disclosure, unified management".
The recruitment process must be carried out in accordance with the announcement, declaration, review, publicity, employment, pre-job training and arrangement for work.
In addition, the new rules also clarify the specific responsibilities of the main development departments for rural public welfare positions, the subsidy standards and methods for rural public welfare positions, and stipulate that each rural public welfare position development department should purchase commercial accident insurance for rural public welfare positions; require relevant departments to regularly supervise the subsidy distribution of rural public welfare positions.
