Let's take a look at some of these "strange hot searches".
What is normal public opinion?
Randomly select three hot searches: February 2nd Dragon Head Raising, Haidilao Price Increase, and the HuoLaLa incident. The public opinion spreads to form a peak, then [the index falls] (smooth curve) eventually dissipates. If secondary public opinion is generated, there will be another small hump.
They look exactly like the [Network Public Opinion Evolution Model] displayed on the official website of the Cyberspace Administration of China.
What is an abnormal public opinion?
Six hot searches in the same event are randomly selected, presenting a [solitary peak], [sawtooth] and [cliff].
[Lone Peak] refers to the rapid rise to the top of the hot search list after artificial heating, which attracts the attention of the public; [Serrated] refers to periodic heating, which ensures that the topic stays on the hot search list; [Cliff] refers to collective evacuation, after the hot search has played its “role”, it is given a new task and sent to a new battlefield.
In Figure 9, the peak of the heat wave of one event is exactly the trough of another event. The time is exactly the same. It must be that a unified batch of water army received the task and started a new round of attack.
The professionalization of black PR is evident: dozens of hot searches simultaneously ranked; which ones attract attention, which ones responsible for popular science, which ones incite war and create momentum, which ones divert attention, which ones affect cognition, which ones mislead judgment, which ones incite emotion, which ones coerce decision-making, black production accounts fight in batches and nodes with fine-tuned operations, almost considering all factors in the spread of public opinion.
Communication is a science. Without subjective factors such as stance and emotion, and based on objective data, black public relations will have nowhere to hide.
Wherever we go, there will be traces left behind. Let's dig them out together.
Data source: Hot Search Time Machine.
Omicron strain infection cases found in Mauritius and other countries for the first time - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, December 12 -- According to comprehensive reports from Xinhua News Agency correspondents stationed abroad, Mauritius, Cyprus and Malawi have recently reported the first cases of infection with the Omicron variant of the COVID-19 virus.
Mauritius reported its first two cases of Omicron infection on October 10.
According to the introduction of the Mauritian Minister of Health Kailash Jagutpal, one of the infected people was a tourist who arrived in Mauritius on November 27 from South Africa; the other infected person was a local resident in Mauritius. He tested positive for nucleic acid on November 30 after contacting a person who had recently returned from South Africa.
After being treated in isolation at the hospital, the nucleic acid test results of these two infected persons turned negative, and they have now returned to their respective residences.
Cyprus Health Ministry announced on the 10th that the country had confirmed three cases of Omicron strain infection for the first time.
The three people were students who returned from overseas travel at the beginning of this month. As they were all mild cases, they did not need hospital treatment.
In order to prevent the spread of the Omicron strain, the government of Cyprus has continuously increased its prevention and control efforts.
From December 6 to January 10 next year, passengers aged 12 and above who enter the country by air will be required to pay for nucleic acid testing at the airport after arrival in Serbia.
On the 10th, the Ministry of Health of Cyprus also announced that it would begin to vaccinate children aged 5 to 11 in the country with the Pfizer COVID-19 vaccine.
Kumbize Chiponda, the Minister of Health of Malawi, said on the 9th that the country had found three cases of infection with the Omicron strain for the first time.
The country's health sector found these three cases of infection by conducting genome sequencing on 12 COVID-19 positive samples collected from November 9 to December 2.
