Is it reliable to buy insurance for a small umbrella?
Little Umbrella is an Internet insurance brokerage platform.
From the perspective of the conditions for establishment: according to the prompt of the Regulations on the Supervision of Insurance Brokerage Institutions (Revised in 2015), to become an insurance brokerage company, it must meet three key conditions: shareholders and sponsors must have no major illegal records in the past three years, the minimum limit is RMB50 million, and it must be approved by the China Insurance Regulatory Commission.
These three requirements are actually very strict. In summary, they require that you have the ability, and be approved by the national authority of the China Banking and Insurance Regulatory Commission (CBIRC), which oversees all insurance companies and banks in China, shareholders must have good conduct, and as an insurance brokerage company, Little Umbrella Insurance, policyholders do not need to question whether Little Umbrella Insurance is legitimate or not, after all, these three thresholds are not something any insurance company can meet.
It's good at this point, it's reliable.
From the perspective of insurance products, Xiaoyuanshu Insurance is an insurance supermarket, and many companies’ star critical illness insurance are sold on this platform, such as the latest He Tai Super Mary No. 5 Critical Illness Insurance, where the claim settlement party and the underwriter are both He Tai Life Insurance, and Xiaoyuanshu Insurance is just a third-party intermediary, so there is no need to question its reliability.
From the perspective of payment mode, the products of Internet platforms have a relatively high cost performance because they have less operating expenses and business staff salary costs. Moreover, the payment method is flexible, supporting monthly payment, reducing the payment pressure of the policyholder, and at the same time, it can maximize the leverage of insurance.
That's a very good thing.
It can be considered.
From the perspective of salesperson professionalism: This is particularly important because insurance is a highly professional industry. Many Internet products can be insured by customers themselves, which will lead to many misunderstandings. In terms of health declaration and occupation, non-insurance practitioners often add their subjective consciousness when insuring, thinking that they are healthy or meet the requirements, which will easily lead to many hidden claims and may be rejected.
I myself have done insurance telemarketing at "Tencent Micro Insurance" (just like Xiao Yu Shuang, it is also an Internet insurance brokerage platform), and I am very responsible to tell everyone.
The insurance on the Internet is real and reliable, but the people are not. The Internet channel has no professional practitioners, and there are also many sales misguidances.
For example, 1 yuan insurance covers 6 million, buy insurance and get a mobile phone, free to receive 60,000 serious illness coverage, these marketing strategies are not wrong, but they avoid the important and avoid the light, will not tell the policyholder, the first month is 1 yuan, the next month is required to charge according to normal, ranging from dozens to 200, many customers do not know what they bought after one or two years of deduction.
They thought they could spend $1 and get $6 million from the insurance company (a piece of cake).
The free mobile phone is only available for special policy numbers, such as 6666 and 8888. And if the winning SMS is sent out, no one will remind you if you don't exchange it.
(For the policyholder, this is another pit.) The free 60,000 yuan critical illness insurance coverage is short-term. If you only rely on this and do not have other commercial insurance, if a critical illness really occurs, what can 60,000 yuan do? It cannot solve the problem, and your future life will begin to be barefoot.
At present, the state is also cracking down on the misleading of Internet insurance sales.
So, overall, the platform is fine and so is the product, but the problem lies in the professionalism and professional ethics of the salesperson.
The topic owner suggested that they should consider carefully. In fact, many offline insurance brokerage companies have a wider range of products, and customers can choose more opportunities and products. Some products are also more cost-effective than Internet products.
I have helped 59 Internet customers to underwrite offline products, saving 2,000-3,000 yuan per person per year.
If you have any questions, please feel free to communicate and exchange with me.
I: Mingya Insurance Broker, with 3 years of experience in enterprise management training, serving nearly a thousand enterprise users and cooperating with more than 100 insurance companies. Before applying for insurance, I will start from the customer's needs, customize insurance products for customers, compare prices for customers during the application process, strive to obtain the best underwriting results for customers, and sort out and manage insurance policies for customers after the application, so that customers can feel at ease.
Grow with every customer for life.
I hope my answer can help you!
According to the definition of the insurance regulatory authorities, Internet insurance is an insurance business in which the policyholder can complete all the insurance application processes after clicking on the insurance application link.
In this process, the policyholder does not need to sign, and the insurance advisor does not need to sign, all steps can be completed by the policyholder.
Although the subscription of Internet insurance does not have much "ceremony", and even there may be no printed paper contract, this does not affect the validity and legal effect of the electronic contract.
This model is similar to the "telemarketing" assembly line, but there is a fatal flaw in this way of purchasing insurance - the follow-up service may not keep up.
Insurance is usually a long-term contract lasting for decades. When we buy insurance, should we not think carefully about whether the "intermediary" we choose is an "insurance intermediary" that can accompany us for a long time and provide us with services many years later?
