Vietnam News Online - Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh attended the Third Vietnam National Digital Technology Enterprise Development Forum
Two major conferences were held during the third Vietnam National Digital Technology Enterprise Development Forum, with topics revolving around digital technology enterprises and national digital transformation, and digital technology enterprises and economic recovery and development during and after the COVID-19 pandemic.
Ruan Mengxiong, Minister of Information and Communications, said that in 2021, despite the continued spread of COVID-19, the number and operating income of Vietnamese digital technology enterprises still maintained growth momentum, reaching nearly 10%.
In 2021, a number of typical digital products were cultivated in Vietnam, which focused on solving major problems faced by Vietnam. Many digital products have gone abroad, and Vietnam's digital technology ranking has been improved.
Minister Ruan Mengxiong called on digital technology enterprises to take responsibility for developing the national digital transformation platform, and the task of developing these national digital platforms is to undertake the national mission.
At the forum, leaders of various departments and state agencies, as well as enterprises, organizations and individuals who are studying, developing, applying and transferring digital technologies, shared their breakthrough ideas and solutions for mobilizing and gathering resources from the whole society to develop Vietnam’s technology enterprises, jointly promote the country’s digital transformation, and promote post-epidemic economic recovery.
Prime Minister Fan Mingzheng emphasized in his speech at the forum that digital transformation is the only way for the world and is an objective requirement for development.
Digital transformation has become a global issue, and digital transformation services are for all, so it is necessary to mobilize the whole nation to participate.
People and enterprises are the core, main body, goal and driving force of digital transformation.
Therefore, all policies should be for the people and enterprises.
Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh stressed that digital transformation should reflect national spirit, and should be based on internal forces, strategic, long-term and decisive factors, while external forces are important and breakthrough points.
He also believed that digital transformation should drive in-depth and sustainable development, participate in the prevention and control of COVID-19, economic recovery and development, respond to subsequent changes, overcome the phenomenon of natural resource depletion, help with green transformation, and develop green energy.
Digital transformation requires participation in the establishment of databases for protecting and promoting national cultural values, historical traditions, and national customs and habits, as well as the promotion of digital transformation in banks, tax, land management and development databases, logistics, and other fields.
The biggest goal of digital transformation is to make people happier and the country more prosperous.
Prime Minister Fan Mingzheng required that all levels of government, all levels of institutions and enterprises should increase leadership and guidance in the development of digital technology, raise awareness of digital transformation, continue to formulate and improve the system of digital transformation, strengthen national management, and promote the development of digital technology enterprises in the spirit of respect, communication, listening, and positive and proactive.
During the forum, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh attended the award ceremony of the 2021 “Made in Vietnam” Excellent Digital Products Award and the opening ceremony of the Made in Vietnam Digital Product Exhibition.
