The Yangtze River mainstream has achieved full coverage of water-based green comprehensive service areas - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Wuhan, December 11 (Reporter Wang Xian) The Chongqing Fuling Water Green Comprehensive Service Area was completed and put into operation as scheduled on December 10. This is the second water green comprehensive service area officially put into operation in the upper reaches of the Yangtze River after the Sichuan Luzhou Water Green Comprehensive Service Area was put into operation on December 8.
Up to now, the water-based green comprehensive service area has covered the upper, middle and lower reaches of the Yangtze River.
Qiu Jianhua, deputy director of the Yangtze River Shipping Administration Bureau of the Ministry of Transport, said that previously, Hubei, Hunan, Jiangxi, Anhui, Jiangsu and other provinces have built and operated 10 water-based green integrated service areas in the middle and lower reaches of the Yangtze River, which have been recognized by the majority of sailors and played an important role in promoting the high-quality development of Yangtze River shipping.
The full coverage of green comprehensive service areas on water is another milestone event in the construction of green shipping on the Yangtze River, and the reception of ship pollutants and shipping services on the Yangtze River have been significantly improved.
According to the introduction, the water green comprehensive service area is an important facility that provides all-round production and living services for ships and crew, and helps crew solve the problems of "urgency, difficulty, anxiety and expectation".
The two water-based green comprehensive service areas in the upper reaches of the Yangtze River, which have been completed and put into operation this time, integrate living services, production services and government services, take green environmental protection as the theme, take ship maintenance and ship emergency rescue services as the characteristics, realize "one-time berthing, multiple services" for ships in the port, and will make the work of crew members who sail on the Yangtze River more efficient and their life more convenient.
Three US aircraft carriers assembled around China, and the most powerful weapon visited Guam rarely. 2022-01-17 Multi-dimensional. The pro-China media reported in multiple dimensions: The latest news of Sino-US relations: The latest satellite images show that three US aircraft carriers are assembling around China; the US media also revealed that one of the most powerful weapons in the US Navy's arsenal visited Guam rarely, sending an important signal to the allies and enemies of the United States in the Indo-Pacific region.
According to the Chinese think tank "South China Sea Strategic Situation Perception Platform", on January 9, the satellite found the US Navy's USS Carl Vinson aircraft carrier near the Balabac Strait.
The Balabac Strait connects the South China Sea and the Sulu Sea, and is a strategic location on the first island chain in the West Pacific Ocean.
The platform predicted that the USS Carl Vinson would be deployed to the South China Sea.
This is the first time that the "Carl Vinson" aircraft carrier has deployed with F-35C fighter jets and CMV-22 Osprey amphibious transport aircraft.
In addition to the Carl Vinson, the US aircraft carrier that is currently cruising in the Pacific Ocean is the USS Abraham Lincoln, which departed from the United States on January 3.
The USS Lincoln also carried the F-35C carrier-based aircraft squadron for the first time, which is affiliated with the 314th Fighter Attack Squadron of the US Marine Corps.
In addition to the above two aircraft carriers, the US Navy currently has the USS Ronald Reagan aircraft carrier, which is docked in Yokosuka, Japan, deployed in the Asia-Pacific region.
The aircraft carrier battle group also includes the missile cruiser "Champlain Lake" and the missile destroyer "Stockdale".
Three US aircraft carriers gather around China, the most powerful weapon rarely visits Guam. On January 17, 2022, the "South China Sea Strategic Situation Perception Platform" released the latest satellite images, showing that three US aircraft carriers are gathering around China.
(Weibo @South China Sea Strategic Situation Perception) The U.S. Navy's three aircraft carriers have gathered in the vicinity of China, and the most powerful weapon has made a rare visit to Guam. On January 17, 2022, the flight route of the U.S. Navy's carrier-based transport aircraft CMV-22B.
(Weibo @South China Sea Strategic Situation Awareness) According to CNN on January 17, one of the most powerful weapons in the US Navy arsenal visited Guam for the first time last weekend.
The Ohio-class nuclear submarine USS Nevada, which carries 20 Trident ballistic missiles and dozens of nuclear warheads, entered the US naval base in Guam on Saturday (January 15).
The three US aircraft carriers gathered around China, and the most powerful weapon made a rare visit to Guam. According to analysts, this is a signal sent to allies and enemies in the increasingly tense situation in the Indian-Pacific region.
This is the first visit of the US ballistic missile submarine to Guam since 2016, and the second public visit to Guam since the 1980s.
Three US aircraft carriers gather around China. The most powerful weapons rarely visit Guam. China has built a large number of military facilities in the Nansha Islands in recent years.
The picture shows Yongshu Island in the Nansha Islands.
(South China Sea Research Forum) The US Navy said in a statement that the visit of the Ohio-class nuclear submarine "Nevada" to Guam strengthened the cooperation between the United States and its allies in the region, showed the ability, flexibility, and combat readiness of the United States, and its continued commitment to the security and stability of the Indo-Pacific region.
Ballistic missile submarines are commonly referred to as "Boomer" submarines.
The whereabouts of 14 "thundering submarines" in the U.S. Navy fleet is usually kept strictly confidential.
The secret surrounding the ballistic missile submarine makes the "booming submarine" the "most important survival weapon in the nuclear triad", and this system also includes the ballistic missile launch shafts in the United States, as well as the B-2 and B-52 bombers that can carry nuclear warheads.
When I told a friend about Meta's recent 26% drop, a $251 billion evaporation, Zuckerberg responded that he was "facing unprecedented competition." Why?
Meta (formerly Facebook) is essentially an advertising company, and its income mainly comes from advertising. Today's advertising companies that make money have their own traffic channels.
Facebook, Instagram, WhatsApp and so on, regardless of what functions they have, are Meta's traffic channels.
In addition, Meta is also the largest "advertising alliance". Many apps connect to Meta's ads, and monetization can be achieved through Meta's advertising platform.
But times have changed.
First, because of the adjustment of Apple's privacy policy, Meta has difficulty in getting user data information, which affects the efficiency of advertising placement.
Apple's current privacy policy is user-friendly, and it will clearly prompt users whether they allow the app to get their information, and most people's normal reaction is definitely not to allow.
If Google pulls another stunt, the impact on Meta's revenue could be even greater.
Second, the China factor in Meta’s previous revenue growth has also weakened (the proportion of this factor is uncertain, but it does exist).
Everyone knows that Meta has no business in China, but this understanding is not accurate.
At least 10% of Meta's revenue comes from China each year, mainly from companies that do business in China.
Meta has about hundreds of employees in its Hong Kong office, and several major agents in the mainland.
Meta is an advertising channel that Chinese companies cannot bypass when they want to expand overseas markets, and most of the money they spend goes to Meta.
Interestingly, Byte's TT is now one of Meta's main competitors, but Meta made a lot of money from Byte in the past two years.
All domestic agents are helping ByteDance to place advertisements on Meta, and Meta’s performance in Greater China is also very good.
I haven't looked at it recently, but I'm sure it's not any better than before.
The stage of Chinese companies burning money overseas on a large scale has passed.
Third, the expansion of new traffic channels is not smooth.
Facebook is getting older and new platforms, including TT, are not in Meta's hands.
The biggest problem is not just the decline in income, but the lack of growth expectations.
The capital market is not only interested in income, but more importantly, it is interested in future expectations.
It's clear Meta's expectations weren't enough.
In order to tell a new story to the market, Zuckerberg talked about the "metaverse".
The metaverse is indeed one of the future directions, but the implementation cycle of the metaverse is relatively long, and this story should not be enough to support Meta’s market value in the next two or three years.
So the next two years should be a difficult period for Meta.
Although Facebook is very prosperous now and has an annual income of $100 billion to $200 billion, in fact, Facebook is now very crisis-stricken. Compared with other Internet companies and high-tech companies, it has no good and safe moat.
Although his several social software now have high daily activity and are mainstream social software, such as Facebook, WhatsApp, etc., Facebook has no confidence in the face of the rapid development of TikTok. The subversion is just a blink of an eye.
The concept of metaverse is out of reach, and there is no hope of success in a short time. Therefore, Facebook is very dangerous. This is also the fundamental reason why Zuckerberg changed the company name and kept looking for new tracks. However, I think his track selection is wrong, and it is a dead end. The above are my thoughts for reference.
Article 17 The state shall implement a registration and practice management system for registered fire engineers.
Those who have obtained the qualification certificate of the first and second level registered fire engineer can practice in the name of the corresponding level registered fire engineer after registration.
Article 18 The Fire Protection Bureau of the Ministry of Public Security is the registration and approval department for first-level registered fire engineers.
The firefighting institutions of the public security organs of provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities directly under the Central Government are the registration and approval departments for the qualification of the second-level registered fire protection engineer, and are responsible for the preliminary review of the registration of the qualification of the first-level registered fire protection engineer.
Article 19 Persons who have obtained the qualification certificates of first-class and second-class registered fire engineers and apply for registration shall be employed by an approved fire technical service institution or a key fire safety unit, and submit the registration application materials to the fire protection agency of the public security organ at the location of the unit (if the employing unit is an enterprise, submit it to the industrial and commercial registration location through the enterprise).
Article 20 After receiving the registration application materials of the applicant, the fire protection institution of the public security organs of the provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities directly under the central government shall inform the applicant of all the contents that need to be corrected at one time on the spot or within 5 working days if the application materials are incomplete or do not meet the statutory form. If the applicant is not informed within the time limit, it shall be accepted from the date of receipt of the application materials.
For the registration application that is accepted or not accepted, a written certificate stamped with the special seal of the fire department of the public security organ at the same level and the date shall be issued.
Article 21 The fire protection institutions of the public security organs of provinces, autonomous regions and municipalities directly under the central government shall complete the preliminary review of the registration application materials of the first-level registered fire engineer and the registration and approval of the second-level registered fire engineer within 20 working days from the date of acceptance of the registration application, and shall report the registration application materials of the first-level registered fire engineer and the preliminary review opinion to the Fire Department of the Ministry of Public Security for approval.
The Fire Bureau of the Ministry of Public Security shall make a decision on whether to approve within 20 working days from the date of receiving the application materials and preliminary review opinions submitted by the fire institutions of provincial public security organs.
If the approval decision cannot be made within the prescribed time limit, the applicant shall be informed of the extended period and reasons.
If a decision is made not to approve, the reasons shall be stated in writing and the applicant shall be informed of his/her right to apply for administrative reconsideration or initiate an administrative lawsuit according to law.
Article 22 The registration and approval department shall issue and deliver the corresponding level of registration certificate within 10 working days from the date of making the approval decision.
Article 23 Each registration certificate shall be valid for three years.
The registration certificate is the practice certificate of the registered fire engineer at the corresponding level during the validity period, and shall be kept and used by the registered fire engineer himself/herself.
Article 24: For initial registration, an application shall be filed within one year from the date of obtaining the qualification certificate for first-level and second-level registered fire engineers.
When applying for initial registration after the expiry of the deadline, the applicant must meet the continuing education requirements of this regulation.
Specific measures for registration management, such as initial registration, renewal registration, change registration, cancellation registration and non-registration shall be separately stipulated by the Ministry of Public Security.
Article 25 Continuing education is a necessary condition for the renewal of registration, re-registration and overdue initial registration of registered fire engineers.
During each registration period, registered fire protection engineers at all levels should complete the corresponding continuing education as required.
Article 26 The registration and approval department shall promptly announce to the public the relevant information of the registered fire engineers, establish a credit file for registered fire engineers, and implement credit management for their practice activities.
Article 27 The registration management department of the qualification of registered fire engineer at all levels shall strictly implement the relevant provisions of the Administrative License Law of the People's Republic of China.
That's all for today's exam information sharing. I hope it can help everyone.
Everyone must work hard to prepare for the exam and strive to pass the fire engineer examination as soon as possible!
