The "Peace Rescue - 2021" Joint Medical Exercise of the Chinese and Vietnamese Armies was successfully concluded - Xinhuanet
Xinhua News Agency, Ha Noi, December 12 (Zhou Na, Teng Huaijin) - On the morning of December 12, all the Chinese participating units in the "Peace Rescue-2021" joint medical exercise between China and Vietnam returned safely to Guangxi, China, marking the successful completion of the seven-day exercise mission.
In this joint exercise, the two armies of China and Vietnam focused on the major topic of humanitarian medical rescue, closely adhered to the mission of logistics and rescue, and completed the contents of joint logistics command, joint on-site rescue, and mass casualty treatment according to the standard of real combat, effectively improving the logistics support capabilities of the two armies.
The results of the exercise were affirmed by both the Chinese and Vietnamese armies.
Ruan Xiongsheng, Director of the Steering Committee for the Vietnamese military exercise, Deputy Director and Chief of Staff of the General Logistics Department of the Vietnamese People's Army, said at the ceremony that ended the exercise that through this exercise, the Vietnamese military doctors learned knowledge about the organization of the exercise and professional activities from the Chinese military doctors, and also saw the medical and support equipment of China.
The results of the exercise proved the professional capabilities of the military medical forces of the two countries in medical assistance and epidemic prevention and control.
Chen Chunming, head of the Chinese Steering and Coordination Group and deputy director of the Health Bureau of the Logistics Support Department of the Central Military Commission, said that this exercise is another pioneering and innovative practice based on the successful joint free clinic in 2018, which has very important milestone significance.
During the exercise, the People's Liberation Army donated medical protective masks, medical protective clothing, rapid nucleic acid testing instruments and other health and epidemic prevention supplies to the Vietnam People's Army.
